# User currency for prices

Retail amounts on the server are often stored as **USD** (`retail_usd`, `retailUsdPerMin`, `cost_usd`, etc.). **Never show `$` / USD to users** unless `billingCurrency == 'USD'`.

## Source of truth

- `AppStore.instance.wallet.billingCurrency`
- `AppStore.instance.wallet.fxMicroPerUsd`

Use `ListenableBuilder(listenable: AppStore.instance, …)` when the UI must update after billing push.

## Formatting

Use helpers in `clients/app/lib/c/ui/money_format.dart`:

| Helper | Use |
|--------|-----|
| `moneyCostLabel(usd, currency:, fxMicroPerUsd:)` | One-off cost |
| `moneyUsdPerMinLabel(usdPerMin, currency:, fxMicroPerUsd:)` | Live / metered **per minute** |
| `moneyBalanceLabel` / `billingCreditBalanceLabel` | Wallet |

Live Call: `liveOfferPricePerMinLocal(offer, currency:, fxMicroPerUsd:)` in `live_offer.dart`.

## Do not

- Hardcode `~\$0.03/min` or `USD` in widgets
- Use `liveOfferPricePerMin` with dollar formatting (removed — local only)

Internal logs, admin, and server-side billing math may stay USD.
